<%#
  "Set up your wallet" — the post-auth step for web3-only onboarding
  (AppFlags.web3_only_onboarding?). Email / Google auth no longer mints a
  custodial web2 wallet, so a freshly signed-in account has no way to transact
  until it links Phantom. This modal is that step.

  WHO SEES IT: WalletSetupPolicy decides, server-side, at sign-in. A user whose
  managed wallet still holds an entry's worth of USDC (>= 19) never sees it —
  they are useable as-is.

  HOW IT OPENS:
    - auto, on the render right after auth success (layout reads the one-shot
      session[:wallet_setup_prompt]), and
    - on demand, when a wallet-less user tries to enter a contest
      (eligibilityBlocker 'wallet_setup_required' -> showWalletSetupModal).

  DISMISSIBLE by design (operator call): closing it leaves the user browsing
  with their picks intact, and the entry gate brings it back when it matters.

  Props (all optional):
    returnUrl — where to land after a successful link (defaults to the current
                page, so the user resumes exactly where they were).

  CRITICAL (Alpine): this partial is cloned from <template x-if="...">, so it
  must have ONE root element, and the x-data attribute below is double-quoted —
  keep every inner string in SINGLE quotes and use no backticks, or the
  attribute closes early and the whole modal silently mounts as a no-op.
%>
<div x-data="{
       get props() { var c = $store.modals.current(); return (c && c.props) || {}; },
       wallets: [],
       connecting: false,
       error: '',
       installUrl: 'https://phantom.com/download',
       // The player starts muted (the only autoplay a browser allows on a modal
       // nobody clicked to open). One click buys sound.
       videoMuted: true,
       // Set when the user leaves for the install page. It puts the row into its
       // waiting state (spinner) and turns the probe below from a single poke
       // into a steady watch.
       installClicked: false,
       // Phantom exists in the BROWSER but not in THIS document — what the probe
       // frame finds. See _probe() for why the two are different things.
       probeFound: false,
       probeTries: 0,
       // Mid-handoff: the page just reloaded to pick up a Phantom it could not
       // reach, and owes the user the signature prompt they asked for.
       resuming: false,
       _resumeTicks: 0,
       _frame: null,
       _onWake: null,
       _onRegister: null,
       _poll: null,
       _probeTimer: null,
       _firstProbe: null,
       init() {
         var self = this;
         this.refresh();

         // Pick up an interrupted connect. resumeConnect() reloads the page to
         // get a document Phantom is actually IN, and the user clicked Connect
         // before that — so finish what they started rather than making them
         // click the same row twice. Read once and clear immediately: a later
         // reload for any other reason must not replay a signature prompt.
         try {
           if (sessionStorage.getItem('walletSetupAutoConnect') === '1') {
             sessionStorage.removeItem('walletSetupAutoConnect');
             this.resuming = true;
           }
         } catch (e) {}

         // WHY THIS POLLS. walletProvider.available() carries an explicit
         // warning in wallet_provider.js -- CALL AT CLICK TIME, because the list
         // fills in asynchronously as wallets register after module load, so
         // reading it during x-data init returns an empty list. Every other
         // consumer honours that by being opened BY a click, late in page life. This modal
         // AUTO-OPENS on the render right after auth — the worst possible moment,
         // mid-handshake — so a single early read is a coin flip: an installed
         // Phantom paints INSTALL, and the user is told to install what they
         // already have, with no way to reach Connect.
         //
         // There is no wallet-registered notification to subscribe to: a wallet
         // that answers our app-ready broadcast just calls register() directly,
         // dispatching nothing. So we listen to the one event that does exist AND
         // poll until the list fills, whichever lands first.
         //
         // NOTE FOR THE NEXT EDITOR: this comment block lives inside a
         // DOUBLE-QUOTED HTML attribute. A single double-quote character
         // anywhere in here closes it and the whole modal mounts as a silent
         // no-op -- it renders, string assertions still pass, and only a browser
         // notices. That is how this very block broke once; keep it quote-free.
         this._onRegister = function() { if (!self.connecting) self.refresh(); };
         window.addEventListener('wallet-standard:register-wallet', this._onRegister);

         // The ping. Free (available() is an array copy), so it runs for as long
         // as the row has no wallet to show and stops the moment it does. It
         // covers every case where the provider CAN appear in THIS document:
         // registration landing late, a locked extension waking up.
         this._poll = setInterval(function() {
           if (self.connecting) return;
           self.refresh();
           self._tickResume();
           if (self.wallets.length > 0) self._stopPoll();
         }, 1000);

         // ...and the half the ping CANNOT do, at all, ever. Chrome injects an
         // extension into documents created AFTER the install and nowhere else,
         // and Phantom ships its provider as a document_start content script
         // with no install-time sweep over open tabs. So in THIS tab — open
         // since before the install — there is nothing for any amount of polling
         // to find, and there never will be. That is why every wallet doc says
         // refresh after installing, and why this modal used to reload the page
         // out from under the user.
         //
         // It does not any more (operator call, 2026-08-18: the page stays put,
         // the row changes). Phantom's manifest also declares all_frames, so a
         // FRESHLY LOADED same-origin iframe does get the provider even inside
         // an old tab — and /wallet_probe is an empty page that exists only to
         // be that frame. Detection now costs one hidden 1px document instead of
         // the whole page.
         //
         // First poke is deferred a beat so the ordinary case never pays for it:
         // if the provider is simply registering late, the ping above wins and
         // no frame is ever created.
         this._firstProbe = setTimeout(function() { self._probe(); }, 1200);

         // Coming back to the tab is the moment worth re-checking: they left to
         // install, and they are back. Cheap now — it pokes the frame, it does
         // not touch the page.
         this._onWake = function() {
           if (document.hidden || self.connecting) return;
           self.refresh();
           self._probe();
         };
         document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', this._onWake);
         window.addEventListener('focus', this._onWake);
       },
       _stopPoll() {
         if (!this._poll) return;
         clearInterval(this._poll);
         this._poll = null;
       },
       _stopProbe() {
         if (this._probeTimer) { clearInterval(this._probeTimer); this._probeTimer = null; }
         if (this._firstProbe) { clearTimeout(this._firstProbe); this._firstProbe = null; }
       },
       _dropFrame() {
         if (!this._frame) return;
         this._frame.onload = null;
         if (this._frame.parentNode) this._frame.parentNode.removeChild(this._frame);
         this._frame = null;
       },
       destroy() {
         this._stopPoll();
         this._stopProbe();
         this._dropFrame();
         if (this._onRegister) {
           window.removeEventListener('wallet-standard:register-wallet', this._onRegister);
           this._onRegister = null;
         }
         if (this._onWake) {
           document.removeEventListener('visibilitychange', this._onWake);
           window.removeEventListener('focus', this._onWake);
           this._onWake = null;
         }
       },
       // Load a brand-new same-origin document in a hidden frame and look for
       // Phantom inside it. A new document is the ONLY thing that makes a
       // just-installed extension appear, and a frame is the only new document
       // we can create without moving the page the user is reading.
       _probe() {
         if (this.probeFound || this.hasPhantom || this.connecting) return;
         // ~5 minutes of watching, then stop. A modal left open all afternoon
         // must not load a document every 2 seconds forever.
         if (this.probeTries >= 150) { this._stopProbe(); return; }
         this.probeTries++;
         var self = this;
         if (!this._frame) {
           var f = document.createElement('iframe');
           f.title = 'Phantom detection';
           f.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
           f.setAttribute('tabindex', '-1');
           // 1px and transparent rather than display:none — it has to actually
           // LOAD, and staying in the layout tree is the version of that no
           // browser is entitled to optimise away.
           f.style.cssText = 'position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:1px;height:1px;opacity:0;border:0;pointer-events:none';
           f.onload = function() { self._readFrame(); };
           this._frame = f;
           this.$el.appendChild(f);
         }
         // Cache-busted: a document served from cache was created BEFORE the
         // install, so it carries no provider and would answer every probe with
         // the same stale no.
         this._frame.src = '/wallet_probe?t=' + this.probeTries;
       },
       _readFrame() {
         var f = this._frame;
         if (!f) return;
         var found = false;
         try {
           var w = f.contentWindow;
           var p = w && (w.phantom || w.solana);
           found = !!(p && (p.solana ? p.solana.isPhantom : p.isPhantom));
         } catch (e) {
           // Cross-origin means the frame is not our probe page any more (a
           // redirect); we simply cannot see, so treat it as not found.
           found = false;
         }
         if (!found) {
           // Nothing yet. Settle into a steady watch, but only once they have
           // actually gone off to install — before that the single poke above
           // is the whole of it.
           if (this.installClicked && !this._probeTimer) {
             var self = this;
             this._probeTimer = setInterval(function() { self._probe(); }, 2000);
           }
           return;
         }
         this.probeFound = true;
         this._stopProbe();
         this._dropFrame();
       },
       refresh() {
         this.wallets = (window.walletProvider && window.walletProvider.available && window.walletProvider.available()) || [];
       },
       // Finish an interrupted connect once the reloaded page has the provider.
       // Bounded: if Phantom does not show up within ~10 ticks the user is left
       // with an ordinary modal rather than a spinner that never resolves.
       _tickResume() {
         if (!this.resuming) return;
         this._resumeTicks++;
         if (this.hasPhantom) { this.resuming = false; this.connect(); return; }
         if (this._resumeTicks > 10) this.resuming = false;
       },
       // Phantom is in THIS document and can be called right now.
       get hasPhantom() {
         return (this.wallets || []).some(function(w) { return w.name && w.name.toLowerCase() === 'phantom'; });
       },
       // Phantom is INSTALLED — reachable here, or seen through the probe frame,
       // or being waited on mid-reload. This is what the row paints, because
       // from the user's side those are one fact: they have a wallet.
       get phantomPresent() {
         return this.hasPhantom || this.probeFound || this.resuming;
       },
       get phantomIcon() {
         var found = (this.wallets || []).find(function(w) { return w.name && w.name.toLowerCase() === 'phantom'; });
         return (found && found.icon) || null;
       },
       get isMobile() { return !!(window.walletProvider && window.walletProvider.isMobile && window.walletProvider.isMobile()); },
       // The row's click. Two ways to finish, one button: if the provider is
       // reachable here, sign now; if it only exists in the browser, this page
       // has to be replaced by one Phantom is in first — so hand the click
       // across that load instead of spending it.
       activate() {
         if (this.connecting || this.resuming) return;
         if (this.hasPhantom) return this.connect();
         if (this.probeFound) return this.resumeConnect();
       },
       // The one page load left in this flow, and it happens where a load is
       // legible: the user pressed Connect, so something is supposed to happen.
       // Both keys are set together — reopen carries the modal across, connect
       // carries the intent — and init() spends them on the other side.
       resumeConnect() {
         this.error = '';
         try {
           sessionStorage.setItem('walletSetupReopen', '1');
           sessionStorage.setItem('walletSetupAutoConnect', '1');
         } catch (e) {
           // Storage blocked: the modal cannot survive the load, so do not start
           // one. Say the one thing that still works.
           this.error = 'Refresh the page to finish connecting Phantom.';
           return;
         }
         this.resuming = true;
         window.location.reload();
       },
       // Link Phantom to the account that just signed in. linkMode routes to
       // /account/link_solana (OPSEC-005 binds the signature to the user id);
       // a guest — this modal should never be open for one, but be safe —
       // falls back to the create-or-login verify path.
       async connect() {
         if (this.connecting) return;
         this.connecting = true; this.error = '';
         var sess = Alpine.store('session');
         var linkMode = !!(sess && sess.loggedIn);
         try {
           var result = await window.solanaConnectAndVerify('Phantom', {
             linkMode: linkMode,
             currentUserId: (sess && sess.userId) || null
           });
           if (result && result.success) {
             if (typeof window.handleSolanaVerifySuccess === 'function') window.handleSolanaVerifySuccess(result);
             // Land back where they were by default, so a user who was mid-
             // lineup returns to their picks instead of /account.
             window.location.href = this.props.returnUrl || window.location.href;
           } else {
             this.error = (result && result.error) || 'Verification failed.';
             this.connecting = false;
           }
         } catch (e) {
           var msg = (e && e.code === 4001) ? 'Signature rejected' : ((e && e.message) || 'Connection failed');
           if (typeof parseSolanaError === 'function') msg = parseSolanaError(msg);
           this.error = msg; this.connecting = false;
         }
       },
       // Ask the player for sound. Spoken over postMessage rather than through
       // the YouTube iframe API script, so this costs no third-party JS on the
       // page: enablejsapi=1 in the src is the whole contract, and the player
       // answers to the same commands either way.
       //
       // Sent twice on purpose. A player that has not finished booting silently
       // drops commands, and this click is the user's only one — the overlay is
       // gone after it, so a dropped unMute would leave them holding a video
       // that stayed silent with nothing left to press.
       unmuteVideo() {
         this.videoMuted = false;
         var self = this;
         var send = function() {
           var frame = self.$refs.videoFrame;
           if (!frame || !frame.contentWindow) return;
           ['unMute', 'playVideo'].forEach(function(fn) {
             frame.contentWindow.postMessage(
               JSON.stringify({ event: 'command', func: fn, args: [] }),
               'https://www.youtube-nocookie.com'
             );
           });
         };
         send();
         setTimeout(send, 400);
       },
       deepLink() {
         var sess = Alpine.store('session');
         var linkMode = !!(sess && sess.loggedIn);
         if (typeof startPhantomDeepLink === 'function') {
           startPhantomDeepLink(linkMode, (linkMode && sess && sess.userId) || null);
         }
       }
     }"
     class="relative">

  <%# Phantom brand sprite (studio-engine). MUST live inside this single root —
      a sibling of the root would be dropped by the host's <template x-if>,
      painting an empty icon. %>
  <%= render "studio/modals/blocks/wallet_brand_sprite" %>

  <div class="relative mb-3 -mt-2">
    <h3 class="text-heading font-bold text-lg leading-tight text-center pt-1">Set up your wallet</h3>
    <%# Dismissible: closing leaves the user browsing with picks intact. %>
    <button @click="$store.modals.close()"
            class="absolute top-0 right-0 -mr-2 text-secondary hover:text-heading text-xl leading-none"
            aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
  </div>
  <%= render "studio/modals/blocks/progress_pill", current: 2, total: 3 %>
  <p class="text-xs text-body mb-4 text-center">
    Turf Monster runs on the Solana public blockchain; you will need a wallet
    to enter contests and collect winnings.
  </p>

  <%# === THE PHANTOM ROW ====================================================
      Installed → Connect (links the wallet to this account). Not installed →
      the install page, same row shape as the wallet-connect picker.

      The two branches carry the two effects the operator specified (swapped to
      this pairing on 2026-08-18), and they say the same thing the badge says,
      louder. The install row wears the rotating studio-team-glow ring in Phantom
      purple: a ring travelling the card's edge reads as a target, and this row
      is the one target on the screen. The installed row PULSES green instead —
      a heartbeat, not a target, because by then the user is not looking for
      what to click, they are being told the thing they went and did WORKED.

      The CONNECT branch also carries one line on what pressing it DOES: a
      first-time user is about to get a signature prompt from a wallet they
      installed five minutes ago, and "sign to prove you own it, no funds move"
      is the difference between clicking and bailing. %>
  <template x-if="phantomPresent">
    <div>
      <button type="button" @click="activate()" :disabled="connecting || resuming"
              style="--pulse-cta-color: rgb(var(--color-primary-rgb)); --pulse-cta-strength: 0.4; --pulse-cta-scale: 1.02"
              class="pulse-cta w-full flex items-center gap-3 p-3 rounded-xl bg-surface-alt border border-strong hover:bg-surface transition text-left disabled:opacity-60 disabled:cursor-wait">
        <img :src="phantomIcon || '/phantom-purple.png'" alt="" class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg">
        <span class="font-semibold text-heading">Phantom</span>
        <span class="ml-auto flex items-center gap-2">
          <span x-show="connecting || resuming" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-secondary"><span class="cta-spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>Connecting…</span>
          <%# Detected: the same green Installed badge the wallet-connect picker
              uses, so a detected wallet reads identically in both places. The
              row is the button — chevron + hover carry the click affordance. %>
          <span x-show="!connecting && !resuming" class="badge border-primary text-primary">Installed</span>
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" class="w-4 h-4 text-muted">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m8.25 4.5 7.5 7.5-7.5 7.5" />
          </svg>
        </span>
      </button>
      <p class="text-[11px] text-muted mt-1.5 px-1">
        Click to connect. Phantom will ask you to sign a message proving the
        wallet is yours — it does not move any funds.
      </p>
    </div>
  </template>
  <template x-if="!phantomPresent">
    <div>
      <%# Not installed. The row wears the glow ring because it is the one
          target on this card. Once the user leaves for the install page a
          spinner appears LEFT of the label: the row is now watching for Phantom — the
          1s ping for this document, the probe frame for the browser — and it
          flips itself to the green Installed badge the moment either finds it,
          WITHOUT reloading the page. The line that appears alongside points at
          the ONLY thing left for the user to do, which is over in Chrome, not
          here — nothing on this card needs pressing again. The row stays a link
          so a user who closed the install tab can re-open it. %>
      <a :href="installUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
         @click="installClicked = true; _probe()"
         style="--studio-team-glow-color: #AB9FF2; --studio-team-glow-thickness: 3px; --studio-team-glow-bloom: 8px"
         class="studio-team-glow w-full flex items-center gap-3 p-3 rounded-xl bg-surface-alt border border-strong hover:bg-surface transition no-underline">
        <svg class="w-9 h-9" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#se-wallet-phantom"></use></svg>
        <span class="font-semibold text-heading">Phantom</span>
        <span class="ml-auto flex items-center gap-2">
          <span x-show="installClicked" class="cta-spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="text-xs text-muted uppercase tracking-wide"
                x-text="installClicked ? 'Waiting…' : 'Install'"></span>
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" class="w-4 h-4 text-muted">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m8.25 4.5 7.5 7.5-7.5 7.5" />
          </svg>
        </span>
      </a>
      <p x-show="installClicked" x-cloak class="text-[11px] text-muted mt-1.5 px-1">
        Finish downloading the Phantom wallet extension.
      </p>
    </div>
  </template>

  <%# Mobile has no extension to install — deep-link into the Phantom app. %>
  <button x-show="isMobile" x-cloak type="button" @click="deepLink()"
          class="mt-2 w-full flex items-center gap-3 p-3 rounded-xl bg-surface-alt border border-strong hover:bg-surface transition text-left">
    <img src="/phantom-white.png" alt="" class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-violet p-1.5">
    <span class="font-semibold text-heading">Open in Phantom app</span>
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" class="ml-auto w-4 h-4 text-muted">
      <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m8.25 4.5 7.5 7.5-7.5 7.5" />
    </svg>
  </button>

  <template x-if="error">
    <p class="text-red-400 text-sm mt-3 text-center" x-text="error"></p>
  </template>

  <%# === NEW TO SOLANA ======================================================
      The teaching half: someone walking the whole install on screen. This was
      two still screenshots and a paragraph explaining what Phantom is until
      2026-08-18; it is a video and one line now, and it plays HERE — a
      half-finished signup should not have to leave the page to find out what a
      wallet is, and should not have to read a paragraph to be told so either.

      IT STARTS ITSELF, SILENTLY (operator call). That is the only autoplay a
      browser permits on a modal that opened without a click, and the trade is
      deliberate: motion earns a glance that a still poster does not, and the
      cost of the glance is nothing, because there is no sound to interrupt what
      the user is doing. The overlay in front of it turns that glance into a
      choice — one click for sound, and the player's own controls after.

      youtube-nocookie, so a video nobody asked for sets no tracking cookie. %>
  <div class="mt-5 pt-4 border-t border-strong">
    <h4 class="text-heading font-semibold text-sm mb-1.5">New to Solana &#129300;</h4>
    <p class="text-xs text-body mb-3">Set up your wallet in <strong class="font-semibold text-heading">90 seconds</strong>.</p>

    <%# The poster sits BEHIND the player as a background rather than in front
        of it, so the block shows the video's own first frame while the iframe
        boots instead of a black rectangle mid-signup. %>
    <div class="relative w-full aspect-video rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-strong bg-black bg-cover bg-center"
         style="background-image: url('<%= WalletSetupHelper::PHANTOM_INTRO_VIDEO_POSTER %>')">
      <iframe src="<%= phantom_intro_video_embed_url %>"
              x-ref="videoFrame"
              title="How to download and set up Phantom"
              class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full"
              allow="autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture; fullscreen"
              referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
              allowfullscreen></iframe>

      <%# The unmute affordance, covering the whole player on purpose: while the
          video is silent EVERY click should mean the same thing, and a click
          that lands on the player instead would pause the video — the opposite
          of what someone reaching for the sound wants. It leaves for good on
          that click, handing the player's own controls straight back. %>
      <button type="button" x-show="videoMuted" @click="unmuteVideo()"
              class="group absolute inset-0 w-full h-full flex items-center justify-center bg-black/20 hover:bg-black/10 transition border-0 cursor-pointer"
              aria-label="Unmute the video">
        <%# CENTRED, over a light scrim. The obvious spot for this chip is the
            bottom corner, and it is the wrong one: YouTube parks its own
            control bar, title and branding along that edge, so the chip lands
            on top of them the moment the player's chrome is showing. The middle
            is the only region of the frame the player leaves empty while
            playing, and the scrim keeps the chip legible over a bright frame. %>
        <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full bg-black/75 px-3 py-1.5 text-[11px] font-semibold text-white shadow-lg transition group-hover:bg-black/90">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" class="w-3.5 h-3.5">
            <path d="M13 4.2a.8.8 0 0 0-1.32-.6L7.4 7.3H4.6A1.6 1.6 0 0 0 3 8.9v6.2a1.6 1.6 0 0 0 1.6 1.6h2.8l4.28 3.7a.8.8 0 0 0 1.32-.6V4.2Z" />
            <path d="M16.4 8.6a.9.9 0 0 1 1.27 0L19.5 10.4l1.83-1.83a.9.9 0 1 1 1.27 1.27L20.77 11.7l1.83 1.83a.9.9 0 1 1-1.27 1.27L19.5 13l-1.83 1.83a.9.9 0 0 1-1.27-1.27l1.83-1.83-1.83-1.83a.9.9 0 0 1 0-1.27Z" />
          </svg>
          Tap for sound
        </span>
      </button>
    </div>

    <%# The escape hatch for anyone who would rather read than watch, and for a
        browser that will not play the embed at all. %>
    <p class="text-[11px] text-muted mt-1.5 text-center">
      <a href="<%= phantom_intro_video_watch_url %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
         class="underline hover:text-secondary">Watch on YouTube</a>
    </p>

    <%# The read-it-instead route — the house /getting-started page once that
        task lands, Phantom's own guide until then (wallet_setup_guide_url).
        Full-size button, neutral tone: it is a real control rather than a link,
        and it must not out-shout the Phantom row above it, which is the one
        thing this modal is actually asking for. %>
    <% guide_url = wallet_setup_guide_url %>
    <% guide_target = wallet_setup_guide_external? ? "_blank" : nil %>
    <% guide_rel = wallet_setup_guide_external? ? "noopener noreferrer" : nil %>
    <a href="<%= guide_url %>" target="<%= guide_target %>" rel="<%= guide_rel %>"
       class="btn btn-neutral w-full mt-3 gap-2 no-underline">
      Detailed Guide
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" class="w-4 h-4">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m8.25 4.5 7.5 7.5-7.5 7.5" />
      </svg>
    </a>
  </div>

  <button type="button" @click="$store.modals.close()" :disabled="connecting"
          class="mt-4 w-full text-center text-sm text-secondary hover:text-heading disabled:opacity-50">
    Maybe later
  </button>

  <%# The card-payment escape hatch, and the ONLY way the Buy an Entry Token
      modal is still reachable from onboarding — that modal used to be where this
      moment landed, and web3-only onboarding (AppFlags.web3_only_onboarding?)
      took its place. Kept small and quiet on purpose: linking Phantom is the
      season's path, and this is the door beside it, not a second front door.

      TWO STATES, because the door only opens for half this modal's audience:

        · WITH a wallet — the grandfathered managed player under 19 USDC. Their
          rails work, so this swaps to the token modal. swap(), not open(): this
          modal is already up, so swapping runs the host's cross-modal slide and
          leaves ONE card on screen instead of stacking two.
        · WITHOUT one — a fresh web3-only signup, which is now most of the people
          who see this card. EVERY entry-token rail refuses them
          (TokensController#stripe_checkout redirects with "Connect a wallet
          first." and navigates them off the contest; #coinflow_order 422s the
          same string into a window.alert), because a token has to be minted
          somewhere. So say that, and do not offer a button that cannot work.
          Kept VISIBLE rather than hidden (operator call, 2026-08-15): the card
          rail is a real option here, one step later, and a control that vanishes
          teaches nothing about why.

      walletConnected is User#solana_connected? — the SAME predicate those rails
      guard on. Not `mode`, which reads 'web2' for a wallet-less account and
      would show the button to precisely the people it refuses. %>
  <template x-if="$store.session.walletConnected">
    <button type="button" @click="$store.modals.swap('buy-entry-token', {})" :disabled="connecting"
            class="mt-2 w-full text-center text-xs text-muted hover:text-secondary disabled:opacity-50">
      Rather pay by card? <span class="underline">Buy an entry token</span>
    </button>
  </template>
  <template x-if="!$store.session.walletConnected">
    <p class="mt-2 w-full text-center text-xs text-muted">
      Rather pay by card? Link a wallet first &mdash; an entry token needs
      somewhere to land.
    </p>
  </template>
</div>
